WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:05.980
Tom, you had an awful lot of thrills at LSU and we all enjoyed a lot of them along with you.

2
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:16.000
But, of course, the one play that I guess will always live in the folklore of LSU is the pass that beat Auburn that you threw to Eddie Fuller.

3
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:22.620
Can you recall what was going on and describe to the people what was happening about that play?

4
00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:29.980
Well, that was a play that had worked for us for a couple of years and we’d had a lot of success with it.

5
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.360
The defense really played well that game.

6
00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:36.580
Auburn was beating up on us, actually, on offense.

7
00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:47.160
And our defense was beating up on their offense and really couldn’t get much going and . . . That was a play that we’d always fallen back on and that was a play that worked for us.

8
00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:54.860
And I was so happy that Eddie got to catch it in the end zone because he had that foot out on the first down.

9
00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:56.640
And finally we got it in on fourth down.

10
00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:05.060
It was just a big play for us and a lot of fans were there and went crazy and all that stuff so . . . It was a big game and a big play for us.

11
00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:07.560
David, backing up to that game with Auburn, now.

12
00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:13.080
When the six points were scored, it was up to you to kick that extra point to win that ball game.

13
00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:20.160
It was kind of odd because I think everybody was figuring the touchdown was seven points so we’d already won the game.

14
00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:29.200
And by the time people had realized that you needed an extra point to make seven, it was already through, so they just continued to cheer.
